messages:  ["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 175648841 and 189371972?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost side (the ones place) and moving to the left:\n\n1. The ones place: \\(1 + 2 = 3\\)\n2. The tens place: \\(4 + 7 = 11\\) (write down 1 and carry over 1)\n3. The hundreds place: \\(8 + 9 + 1 (carried) = 18\\) (write down 8 and carry over 1)\n4. The thousands place: \\(8 + 7 + 1 (carried) = 16\\) (write down 6 and carry over 1)\n5. The ten-thousands place: \\(4 + 1 + 1 (carried) = 6\\)\n6. The hundred-thousands place: \\(5 + 3 = 8\\)\n7. The millions place: \\(7 + 8 = 15\\) (write down 5 and carry over 1)\n8. The ten-millions place: \\(1 + 1 (carried) = 2\\)\n\nSo, combining all these results we get:\n\n- The ones place gives us 3.\n- The tens place gives us 1 and we carried over 1 to the next place.\n- The hundreds place gives us 8 after adding the carry.\n- The thousands place gives us 6 after adding the carry.\n- The ten-thousands place gives us 6 without any carry.\n- The hundred-thousands place gives us 8.\n- The millions place gives us 5 and we carried over 1.\n- The ten-millions place gives us 2 after adding the carry.\n"]
